Defer-block LIFO ordering
=========================

`defer stmt` queues a statement to run when the enclosing
function exits. Multiple defers run in last-in-first-out
order, and the deferred bodies are re-evaluated at exit time
(not captured at defer-time), so reads of mutable state see
the value as of exit, not as of the defer site.

To observe the order from a `#test` (which itself owns the
function scope where the defers would fire — meaning the
asserts inside the test would run *before* the defers do),
we push the defers into a helper function that mutates state
through a pointer. The test then asserts the assembled
state after the helper returns.

If a backend miscompiles defer ordering (eager FIFO, missed
defers, wrong scope chain), the assembled string diverges
from the expected `"321"` and the test fails.

    module sysl.tests.lang_features

    struct Trace
        s: string

    fill_trace(t: *Trace) -> unit
        defer t.s = t.s + "1"
        defer t.s = t.s + "2"
        defer t.s = t.s + "3"

    #test
    test_defer_lifo() -> unit
        var t = Trace("")
        fill_trace(&t)
        assert(t.s == "321", s"expected '321', got '${t.s}'")
